Now game.js.

Persistent functions:
```js
const SAVE_KEY='sporefall.save.v1';
function loadSave(){ try{ return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(SAVE_KEY))||null }catch{return null} }
```

Game constructor:
```
this.canvas = document.getElementById('stage');
this.renderer = new Renderer(this.canvas);
this.input = new Input();
this.audio = new AudioEngine(saved?.muted || false);
this.input.onPauseKey = () => this.handlePauseKey(); // but step also handles pressed pause. Duplicate triggers: onPauseKey triggers immediate; step sees pressed too. Avoid double. Use only step for pause? If keydown happens between steps, step handles. Remove onPauseKey.
```
I added onPauseKey in Input; but can skip setting it. Use step handling.

Menu overlays with buttons; clicking Play starts. Need pointer events to not propagate to game; overlays cover.

`resize()`: compute view scale, canvas size, camera view.

```
resize(){
 const w = window.innerWidth, h = window.innerHeight;
 this.dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio||1, 2);
 this.canvas.width = Math.round(w*this.dpr);
 this.canvas.height = Math.round(h*this.dpr);
 this.canvas.style.width = w+'px'; ...
 const aspect = w/h;
 let scale = Math.min(w/1000, h/560);
 if (aspect < 0.95) scale = w/500;
 scale = Math.max(0.55, Math.min(scale, 2.2));
 this.scale=scale;
 this.viewW = w/scale; this.viewH = h/scale;
 this.renderer.resize(w,h,this.dpr,scale)?? Renderer just uses canvas dims and game.scale.
 this.snapCamera();
}
```
Renderer draws using ctx.setTransform(dpr*scale...). Canvas pixel dims w*dpr. Good.

Camera:
```
computeBounds(){
 if (bossActive) { const a=level.arenaData; return {x0:a.x0-50, x1:a.x1+50, y0:a.groundY-700, y1:a.groundY+80};}
 return {x0:0, x1:level.widthPx, y0:0, y1:level.heightPx};
}
updateCamera(dt, snap=false){
 const p=this.player;
 let targetX = p.cx + p.facing*60 - viewW/2;
 let targetY = p.cy - viewH*0.56;
 const b=this.cameraBounds || default;
 let minX=b.x0, maxX=b.x1-viewW;
 if (maxX<minX) targetX=(b.x0+b.x1)/2 - viewW/2 else clamp
 Similarly Y; if viewH>height, center: targetY = b.y1 - viewH? show bottom? For portrait, level bottom at ground+below; we want ground near bottom: y = level.heightPx - viewH (shows sky above). Let's set minY = Math.min(b.y0, b.y1 - viewH) and maxY = Math.max(b.y0, b.y1 - viewH). If viewH > level height, y fixed = b.y1-viewH (negative), showing sky. Good.
 Smoothing: this.camera.x = damp(...,7,dt), y damp 6.
 Shake handled in renderer.
}
```
Arena bounds for camera when boss: x0=a.x0-60, x1=a.x1+60, y1=a.groundY+40, y0=a.groundY-700. view width 1000; arena 1248 → can pan; clamp. For bat queen flying high, camera fixed vertical since player on ground; view from ground-~600. Fine.

Lookahead only when moving? Use facing*50.

Title camera: set camera over spawn; pan oscillates. On title, updateCamera with custom pan: `panX = spawn.x - viewW*0.35 + Math.sin(time*0.08)*140`; clamp 0..level width; y = groundY - viewH*0.7. Do in updateTitle.

Level loading:
```
loadLevel(i, {title=false}={}){
 this.levelIndex=i;
 this.level=buildLevel(i);
 this.player=new Player(level.spawn.x, level.spawn.y, this.armor);
 this.enemies=level.enemies.map(d=>new Enemy(d,this));
 this.pickups=level.pickups.map(d=>new Pickup(d));
 this.projectiles=[]; this.particles=[]; this.texts=[];
 this.ambient=createAmbient(level);
 this.boss=null; this.bossActive=false; this.bossDead=false;
 this.checkpoint={x:level.spawn.x,y:level.spawn.y};
 this.level.checkpoints.forEach(c=>c.active=false);
 this.cameraBounds=null;
 this.state = title?'title':'playing';
 this.music theme start.
 snap camera.
 updateHUD; hide prompt; hide boss bar.
 if(!title){ showLevelCard(); saveProgress(); fadeIn...}
}
```
The title screen needs level loaded before render. In constructor, load title.

But when starting from title, we reload level 0 with a new player (title player exists); fine.

Save progress at level start: {levelIndex, armor, spores, deaths, muted, completed:false}. But "Continue" should maybe restore checkpoint? Not necessary.

`saveProgress()` also stores totalSpores? Save `spores` current only; on continue, set totalSpores=spores for stats. Fine.

Start:
```
startRun(fresh=true){
 this.audio.init();
 if(fresh){ this.spores=0; this.armor=0; this.deaths=0; this.totalCollected=0; this.runTime=0; this.levelIndex=0; this.completed=false; }
 hide title; show hud; this.loadLevel(this.levelIndex); this.state='playing'; this.showLevelCard(); 
}
```
Continue uses save fields.

`bindUI`:
- playBtn click → startNew
- continueBtn → continue
