content.text:
Now add helper methods after drawTiles (before drawArenaWall). Need `groundTexture`, `drawGroundSurface`, `drawEdgeRoot`, `drawPlatform`.

Be careful: groundTexture uses this._groundTex key; `this.ctx.createPattern` each theme once. Pattern must be recreated when canvas transform? No.

Colors: for body pattern, base fill theme.ground. Add texture. Need pattern continuity across tiles; createPattern and fillRect per tile samples world coords; yes.

Make sure pattern doesn't include a border seam; use full 128x128 and wrap elements partially? Drawing shapes that cross edge won't wrap automatically, causing seams. Keep all shapes inside a 6px margin; patterns repeat with slightly regular gaps but fine. To wrap, draw each at x±128/y±128 duplicate for shapes near edges. Simpler keep shapes inside 4..124. Specks near edges okay too (dots).

Write:
```
groundTexture() {
 const key = this.level.theme;
 if (this._groundTexKey === key) return this._groundTex;
 const c = document.createElement('canvas');
 c.width = 128; c.height = 128;
 const g = c.getContext('2d');
 const { ground, groundDark, cap, edge } = this.theme;
 g.fillStyle = ground; g.fillRect(0,0,128,128);
 // mottling
 for (let i=0;i<22;i++){...}
 // strata lines
 for (let i=0;i<4;i++){ g.strokeStyle = rgba(groundDark, .25); ... horizontal wavy }
 // roots vertical
 for...
 // pebbles/specks
 ...
 this._groundTex = this.ctx.createPattern(c, 'repeat');
 this._groundTexKey = key;
 return this._groundTex;
}
```
`rgba` expects hex; theme colors are hex. Good.

drawGroundSurface:
```
const ctx, theme, T
// cap base with slightly wavy top edge? We can draw cap as rounded top? Ground top flush.
ctx.fillStyle = theme.cap; fillRect(x, y, T, 12);
ctx.fillStyle = theme.cap2; fillRect(x, y, T, 3.5);
// moss clumps below
for i 0..3 ellipse ...
// shadow under
ctx.fillStyle = rgba(groundDark,.4); fillRect(x, y+12, T, 3)
// grass blades above
for i 0..5:
 bx = x + 3 + hash(...)*(T-6)
 bh = 4 + hash(...)*11
 slope = (hash-0.5)*6
 ctx.strokeStyle = i%2 ? rgba(cap2,.75) : rgba(cap,.85)
 lineWidth 1.4
 beginPath moveTo(bx, y+1); quadraticCurveTo(bx+slope*.4, y-bh*.6, bx+slope, y-bh); stroke
// occasional flower
if hash(tx*11.3) > .9: draw stem + petals in warm color, glow? tiny.
```
Careful flowers on every 10th tile—nice.

drawEdgeRoot:
```
const len = 10 + hash(tx*3.7+ty*1.9)*22;
ctx.strokeStyle = rgba(theme.groundDark, .7); lineWidth 1.5;
beginPath moveTo(px, y+12); bezierCurveTo(px+dir*6, y+22, px-dir*4, y+len, px+dir*2, y+12+len); stroke
```
But root at every side tile (left edge runs whole height each tile) may be too busy; use hash condition: if hash(tx*5.1+ty*7.7) > 0.45 draw. Also draw second shorter root. Root starts at y+12 each tile so repeating along vertical edge; looks like hanging roots. Fine.

drawPlatform:
```
const themeKey = this.level.theme;
const x,y,T
if (themeKey === 'forest') {
  ctx.fillStyle=platformDark; posts...
  board
  top
  grain lines
  moss top clumps
  vines if hash>0.5
} else if cavern {
  // brackets? draw slab with rough underside
  board roundRect maybe x-1 y w T+2 h 14 r 3
  top lip
  // jagged under: 3 triangles
  // crystal under on some tiles
} else {
  slab; top; snow; icicles
}
```
Boards are continuous tiles; roundRect per tile creates visible gaps/seams at tile edges? Existing code draws x, T+1 rounded corners each tile → a series of pill shapes with tiny notches. Screenshots show a continuous bar? It looked like continuous with small segments, acceptable but better to make continuous: draw rectangle with roundRect only at platform run edges. Need know if neighbor is '='. Use level.charAt(tx-1,ty) and tx+1. Board x offset: if left neighbor platform, x-0.5; else round left. Simpler: draw rect x, y, T+0.5, 15, then if left edge round top-left. Canvas roundRect supports individual radii? custom. Eh.

Keep per-tile rounded segments but make width T+1 and overlap so seams hidden. Use fillRect for the main board and add rounded caps only at run ends:

```
const leftEnd = level.charAt(tx-1,ty) !== '=';
const rightEnd = level.charAt(tx+1,ty) !== '=';
ctx.fillStyle=platform; ctx.fillRect(x - (leftEnd?0:0.5), y, T+1, 15);
if (leftEnd) { roundRect(ctx,x,y,T,15,5) }...
```
Simplest: fill rect full width, then if end caps draw roundRect at ends; corners visible. Existing look okay though. I'll draw continuous:

```
ctx.fillStyle = platform;
ctx.beginPath();
const capL = level.charAt(tx-1,ty)!=='=';
const capR = level.charAt(tx+1,ty)!=='=';
// manually path with rounded outer corners
```
That's more code. Alternative: use roundRect(x-0.5, y, T+1, 15, 4) every tile; overlaps hide seams except top highlight line breaks. It's fine, looks like planks.

Forest wood grain: 1-2 horizontal lines per tile at y+6, y+11 with alpha .15, varying lengths.

Moss: green clumps top at some tiles (cap/cap2).

Vines: stroke from x+hash*T, y+15 downward with sway, length 6-28; tiny leaves.

Cavern: slab with platformTop top 4; jagged underside triangles in platformDark; crystals: 20% chance draw small diamond glow below. Also vertical crack lines.

Summit: slab with pale top; snow cap (cap2) 3px; icicles under at deterministic positions with theme.spike, alpha .5.

Add supports:
- Forest: only draw posts on tiles where hash(tx*3.1)>.45? Could use alternating: draw two posts every tile currently; keep but shorten and vary.
- Cavern/summit: no posts, floating looks okay for magical platforms? Screenshot summit platforms had legs making them look like tables. Removing helps. But then how are platforms held up? In cavern/summit they can be floating stone/magic. Fine. Could add subtle glow underside instead.

