- far layer: rgba(theme.near,.55)
- near layer: rgba(theme.groundDark,.9) maybe dark enough.
On summit groundDark #1a1b2f; silhouette visible against bg #232a52; good.
Forest groundDark #16261e on bottom dark #040a08; might be too dark; cap/edge color could rim highlight. Add rim light: draw same shape offset? We can add stroke with theme.cap alpha.

Perhaps use `theme.near` for far and `theme.groundDark` near, with a subtle top rim using theme.edge at 0.15. Good enough.

